  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Windham Thomas Wyndham-Quin, fourth Earl of Dunraven, was an Anglo-Irish landowner whose inherited estates drew their principal income from Welsh coal. He helped negotiate the agreement behind Ireland's Wyndham Land Act and twice challenged for the America's Cup. His published work ranged from travel and navigation to Irish affairs and autobiography.",
    "html": "<p>Windham Thomas Wyndham-Quin, fourth Earl of Dunraven, was an Anglo-Irish landowner whose inherited estates drew their principal income from Welsh coal. He helped negotiate the agreement behind Ireland's Wyndham Land Act and twice challenged for the America's Cup. His published work ranged from travel and navigation to Irish affairs and autobiography.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 51,
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Institutional biographies establish the principal income, legislative negotiations, competition record and sustained publications."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2"
    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "The fourth Earl of Dunraven brought plants from different continents together in the gardens of Garinish Island. He used the island's alternating limestone ridges and gorges to shape the planting, setting red Himalayan rhododendrons and New Zealand cabbage palms alongside native oak. Mauve rhododendrons from eastern Europe added another colour to the garden.\n\nDuring the First World War, Dunraven equipped a steam vessel as a hospital transport and personally commanded it in the English Channel and Mediterranean. He undertook this service while already in his seventies and received an OBE for his work.",
    "html": "<p>The fourth Earl of Dunraven brought plants from different continents together in the gardens of Garinish Island. He used the island's alternating limestone ridges and gorges to shape the planting, setting red Himalayan rhododendrons and New Zealand cabbage palms alongside native oak. Mauve rhododendrons from eastern Europe added another colour to the garden.</p>\r\n<p>During the First World War, Dunraven equipped a steam vessel as a hospital transport and personally commanded it in the English Channel and Mediterranean. He undertook this service while already in his seventies and received an OBE for his work.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 93,
